=== consequence for the short-circuit order ===
  A conjunction should test cheapest-first, but 'cheapest' flips with length, so the order
  must be chosen per target from the measured curve rather than fixed. And the ratio that
  justified adding ShapeKnots at all -- cheapest AND strictest -- holds only where it is
  actually cheapest; above that band it buys the same strictness at a higher price.

=== consequence for every dollar figure on this branch ===
  ShapeKnots median 49 ms below 35 nt against 344 ms above 50 nt (7.1x). The USD numbers in metric.py used oracle-SECONDS measured
  per attempt, so they are unaffected -- those were realised times, not modelled from a
  constant. What WAS wrong is every statement of the form 'ShapeKnots costs 0.31x pKiss'.
